Subject: [PATCH v2 0/13] hv: vmbus: make rings and host-visible buffers
 survive buddy fragmentation

Michael Kelley's review of the original vzalloc() fallback explains why
CCA and TDX guests without a paravisor need direct-map page transitions.
This revision uses the existing chunk allocator and keeps allocation,
GPADL ownership and mapping references together.

This is an unsent validation snapshot. The thirteen-stage architecture
builds pass for these exact code mails. Changed-byte live mainline runtime
and the final review remain pending.

References:
  Initial proposal: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/09/18/276
  Review:
    https://www.mail-archive.com/linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org/msg2658605.html
  Allocator discussion:
